WEBVTT

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:16.240
RULES OF THE PRETTY BOY DETECTIVE CLUB
1. BE PRETTY. 2. BE A BOY. 3. BE A DETECTIVE.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.160
This episode, we're bringing you
a story about an election.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:29.250
THE ELECTION OF THE NEXT
STUDENT COUNCIL PRESIDENT

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.880
It's the election to choose
the next student council president.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:29.630
Of course, I say "student council election,"
but what's being held is basically a rigged one.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.260
There's no doubt that
the current vice-president Wana Naganawa

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:38.480
would follow in the current president's
footsteps and move up to the role of president.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.940
So, as a representative
of the unaware students,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.820
I honestly had close
to no interest in this election.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.280
Make no mistake...

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.700
Make no mistake that yours truly,
someone like me,

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.080
someone lowly like me,
someone at my level,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.740
that I would...

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.790
In other words, for me to become the candidate
for the next student council president...

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.750
This is simply the worst.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.870
MELANCHOLY OF
THE STUDENT 
COUNCIL PRESIDENT

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:08.630
What? I was thinking
you haven't shown up in a while,

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:12.380
and when you do, you're in a bad mood,
Mr. Student Council President.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.720
This time, I really am at my wit's end.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:21.020
I don't get it. The election campaign
is going well, isn't it?

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.520
You're basically done
locking in your votes, aren't you?

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.650
Yes. I had more or less locked down votes
outside of your group, Michiru.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:32.780
I know, right?
The minority voice won't be heard.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.910
There aren't any noteworthy candidates
other than Naganawa, either.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:39.160
Yes. And about Miss Naganawa....

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:45.380
She got into a traffic accident the other
day, and is currently hospitalized.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.090
WANA NAGANAWA

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.050
Wana Naganawa.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.560
Class 2-A.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.680
Student number... That, I don't know.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.270
Anyway, she's the vice-president of
the Student Council Executive Department,

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.400
and her nickname is Snow Queen.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.570
In a good way.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.780
She's not in any critical condition.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.950
After about a month's stay in the hospital,
she should be back to normal,

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.200
and can resume her academic work.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.210
Hospital? A month?

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:50.290
Huh? Then what will she do
about the election?

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.630
That's what makes this the worst thing.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:56.470
Miss Naganawa must withdraw her candidacy.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:04:01.970
If Miss Naganawa is unable to be a candidate,
that means there'll be a change in regime.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.140
And that's the worst part of it.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.180
But isn't that...

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.190
...something that just can't be helped?

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:11.310
Mayumi.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:16.400
This lolicon isn't lamenting the fact
that he's going to lose power.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.410
He's lamenting that someone else
will become student council president.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:23.200
What's that about? How is that any different?

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.580
Basically, if anyone other than Naganawa,

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.750
who's been assisting Nagahiro,
becomes student council president,

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:32.840
there's no way that said person could be
on equal footing with the academy.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.000
Oh, I see, that's what you mean.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.720
Yubiwa Academy once
valued freedom and individuality,

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.760
but with each new year,
they prioritize efficiency,

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.180
and tighten the reins on their students.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.140
The people who gathered the students'
opinions against such a movement

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.600
was the current Student Council
Executive Department,

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.560
in other words, the Sakiguchi regime.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:05:00.240
For Mr. Senpai, of course, such a structure
would be desired after his retirement.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.070
To keep the equilibrium between
the academy and its students intact.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.240
That's probably why he decided
to endorse the vice-president,

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:12.830
but those plans tragically came
crumbling down due to a traffic accident.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:15.040
This is the worst.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.920
Yes. Miss Naganawa
is depressed about this as well.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.590
She's more dejected about

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:24.470
how she has to withdraw from
the race more than the accident itself.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.680
Why not have another member

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.270
of the Student Council Executive
Department become a candidate?

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:36.110
If push comes to shove, that's what I'd probably
have to do, but I can't force them to do so.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:37.570
Force them?

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:41.740
Aren't the members of the Executive Department
completely obedient to your orders?

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:42.990
Your manner of speech.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.370
That's precisely why
I cannot force them, Miss Mayumi.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:54.750
If they became candidates for the student
council president to continue my stance,

00:05:56.290 --> 00:06:00.050
and got into another traffic accident,
I would be too ashamed of myself.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.430
If they got into another traffic accident?

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:04.930
"Another"?

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.010
ANOTHER

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:06.100
Come on now.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.010
That makes it sound like Naganawa

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.640
got into a traffic accident because she became

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.640
a candidate for the next
student council president.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.900
Can such a thing happen?

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.020
TRAFFIC ACCIDENT AT D HILL

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:27.240
Who was the driver of the car
that ran over Naganawa?

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.660
It was a hit-and-run.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.120
The culprit hasn't been apprehended yet.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.500
Hit-and-run...

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.960
Aren't there any witnesses?

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:39.250
Unfortunately, it was
a traffic accident at D Hill.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.500
D Hill.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:52.180
YUBIWA ACADEMY

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:49.260
It's the D Hill from "A Hill,
B Hill, C Hill, and D Hill."

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:52.180
A HILL

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:52.180
B HILL

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:52.180
C HILL

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:52.180
D HILL

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:52.100
The letters are in order of traffic,
with A Hill being the busiest.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:56.350
In other words, D Hill
is the least popular around here.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:56.430
D HILL

00:06:56.690 --> 00:07:01.070
Oh, but as the victim, Naganawa
might remember something, right?

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:08.240
Unfortunately, she doesn't remember
much of the accident itself.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.830
In any case, as long as
such a danger is a reality,

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:16.580
he's unable to easily find
a replacement for Naganawa.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:22.340
But are you okay with this, Mr. Senpai?

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:26.840
That's basically giving in
to the enemy's foul tricks.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:31.760
Enemy? Well, that's only
if such a faction exists.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.730
You shouldn't be giving in to such threats.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.980
I'm sure the Executive
Department members...

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:44.530
will declare candidacy without
thinking twice about the danger.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.860
If it were me, I would do so without a doubt!

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.160
This is what you call
acting upon your emotions.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:57.580
I'd thought that you would
definitely say that, Miss Mayumi.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:01.790
That's why I would like
to plead my case to you.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:06.420
As a mission for the Pretty Boy Detective Club,
from the club vice-president...

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:07.800
What now?

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.880
CANDIDACY INFILTRATION

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.100
No, no, no, no, I can't possibly do it!

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.970
I can understand your feelings

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:20.810
of wanting to rely on your underclassman
who you have full confidence in!

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.820
Oh no, you were the only underclassman

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:26.150
who I can think of that I didn't
mind having being run over.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:32.320
True, if it were Mayumi, and she ends up
getting run over from some conspiracy,

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.700
that would be the best outcome in its own way.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:38.830
It's pretty rare when you can say to someone
that you don't mind them being run over.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:38.910
{=0}JUST RUN OVER ME ALREADY

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:42.500
No, but you shouldn't
run over anyone to begin with.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.460
But from a more practical standpoint,
I don't think I would cut it.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:51.300
Even if I were to be a candidate,
who would actually vote for me?

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.810
Don't worry about that.
I will officially endorse you.

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.390
Mr. Delinquent should just volunteer.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.020
He's got support as the Bossman, right?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:05.730
Let's say Nagahiro were to back me up.
Who's going to believe that?

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.030
Oh, I see.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:12.700
Then, well, what about
Mr. Bare-Legs or Mr. Genius?

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:18.580
Saying so, I had to admit that both of them
would be unreasonable as well.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:21.750
In the first place, the members
of the Pretty Boy Detective Club

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:25.250
have no relationships outside the art room.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.960
Oh, that's right. Our leader...

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:30.880
Nothing.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.550
I will get run over.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:38.310
So, please make sure to find out who this
culprit is, the "hit-and-run driver of D Hill."

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:42.350
You won't get run over.
We'll properly protect you from that.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:49.230
1. TO MAKE ME WIN THE ELECTION

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:48.980
And so, there are currently two missions
for the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:55.240
2. FIGURE OUT WHO WAS THE
'HIT-AND-RUN DRIVER OF D HILL.'

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:55.120
and figure out who was the
"hit-and-run driver of D Hill."

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:59.450
THE NEXT MORNING

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.330
The next morning...

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.370
"ELECTION STRATEGY"

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.290
"HAH HAH HAH"

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.170
I heard the story, Mayumi Dojima!

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:10.760
Just how far does your self-sacrifice
and beautiful spirit extend?

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:12.550
Stop hugging me.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:18.720
As part of the physical group, do I plaster
myself on Mayumi and be her bodyguard?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.600
Stop plastering against me in real life.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:27.110
And we can't leave the police to
determine who did the hit-and-run, right?

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:30.190
I see! So determining the perpetrator
is also a mission.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.650
I'll leave the deduction up to you, Michiru!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:36.620
And I'll come up with an election
strategy. Isn't that right, Leader?

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:37.910
Yes.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:44.290
That's right. From today, Mayumi's
cross-dressing should be done by Sosaku.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:49.960
Let's visualize Mayumi's inner beauty such
that everyone can see for themselves.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:53.590
That about sums up how we'll split our roles.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:56.470
So where do we actually stand, Nagahiro?

00:10:56.470 --> 00:11:00.260
Realistically analyzing this, does our
gloomy kid have any chance of winning?

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.100
There is a chance of winning.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:10.070
However, I'm guessing
that it'll be quite a close contest.

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:12.190
Does she have any rivals?

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:14.650
Analyzing the situation up until now,

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:19.070
I think the most powerful opponent
is Yokuya in class 2-B.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.330
Class B?

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:23.450
That's the class I'm in.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.530
CLASS 2-B

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:29.290
But was there a guy
named "Yokuya" in there?

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:36.970
It somehow feels wrong that such a student who
lacked presence is the current top candidate.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:40.010
Yes. I did investigate a bit as well,

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:43.640
but he doesn't seem to be a student
who is especially strange.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:47.730
If I had to say anything, his characteristic
is the lack of characteristics.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:52.020
It seems he isn't doing anything
for his election campaign either.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.570
Maybe he is doing something.

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:58.990
He's now the top candidate
because Naganawa was hospitalized.

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:04.950
That means in some way, he's the one who
gained the most from the accident on D Hill.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:05.070
SUSPICION

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.580
SUSPICION

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:16.090
Well, I'm not saying that this Yokuya guy
is the "hit-and-run driver of D Hill."

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:18.880
If you decide that you actually want to go
through with a hit-and-run,

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.890
you have to procure a car.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:24.060
It's just as Miss Mayumi says.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:29.390
I don't think that Yokuya, a middle school
student, would be able to procure a car.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:30.440
However...

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:35.110
If a student like him
were to become student council president,

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:38.530
there's a possibility that it'll
be convenient for a certain faction.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.450
That idea should be considered.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:43.740
Even if you suppose
it was Yokuya's election campaign,

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.410
do you think someone else acted upon it?

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.910
Don't overthink it too much.

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:51.830
Suspicion turning into idle fear
is the worst thing that can happen.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:55.210
The possibility that everything
is a misunderstanding is the highest.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.170
Did you finish all
the complicated talk?

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.010
Then let's begin our activities!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.640
Apparently he can't hear
any discussions that aren't beautiful.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:10.640
Today, we shall be pretty, we shall be boys,
and we shall be detectives!

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:14.190
And we shall be the best team.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:18.070
Even in the worst situation,
we have to be the best team.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:25.580
It seems my rival's full name
is Kinshiro Yokuya.

