00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.790
I had completely forgotten about it.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:33.880
Not only his name,
but also his surname, or rather

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:35.880
that he sat next to me.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.720
Seriously? So you're my rival?

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:41.050
Well, that's okay.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.300
It'll be quite convenient for observing you.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.970
I'm sorry! I forgot my textbook!

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:51.100
Yokuya, would you mind if I looked at yours?

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.310
Yay!

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:56.150
Here you go.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:59.570
Um, so you... What was your name?

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:01.570
D-Dojima.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:07.160
Huh? That voice, can it be that you're a girl?

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:09.240
Well, yeah.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.000
Oh, I see.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.080
Y-Yeah. Good to know you.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.340
His hair looks slightly
bleached and is cut short.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.680
He properly wears his uniform.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:26.600
However, he wears his tie a bit loosely.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:32.310
For the most part, his appearance is not untidy,
but it's not like he's fastidious either.

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:35.440
It's like he has personality, but he doesn't.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:38.690
His image is that of a middle school student.

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:43.030
You could say he's a collage of
"this is what a middle school kid is like."

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:47.450
It's not that he lacks personality,
but his personality is lacking thereof.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:49.950
His lack of features is his feature.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:54.120
His feature is the lack of features
and nothing catches attention.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:57.840
Why did someone who's lacking in individuality,
or rather un-individualistic as Yokuya,

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:01.300
decided to be a candidate for
the student council president election?

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:07.260
Furthermore, when he first announced his
candidacy, it was almost surely a losing fight.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:10.010
Despite the situation,
he's courageously making his run.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:14.730
It makes me feel like
Yokuya has some sort of goal.

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.150
It's fine if that turns out to
be a great ambition,

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:20.520
or a desire of wanting to
become student council president

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:24.950
so he can have a good time being pampered.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:28.660
But it feels like he has
an exceptional circumstance.

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:29.910
But...

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:33.870
Such an abnormal characteristic,
or a unique individualism,

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:39.170
was not felt at all for better or for worse
from the boy sitting in the seat next to me.

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:41.460
What exactly is up with this guy?

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.090
Nope, not good.

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:45.760
By becoming a member
of the Pretty Boy Detective Club,

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:49.260
I'd been basking in the feeling
that I had become a special person,

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:54.060
and I'd been looking down on what you call
"normal middle school students" in some way.

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:56.310
This is a huge problem.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:58.310
He indeed seems like a middle school boy.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:02.150
But of course he would
if he's a middle school boy.

00:16:02.150 --> 00:16:04.150
That's when I had a thought.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.570
I don't have to make an effort
to announce my candidacy.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:11.660
And Mr. Senpai doesn't have to make the effort
to support a candidate taking Naganawa's place.

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:16.290
If the elected Yokuya, or whoever else it may
be, could be convinced right after the election,

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:19.290
wouldn't that work everything out peacefully?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:24.170
To do that, I felt that it'd be better for me
at this point to have interactions with Yokuya

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:28.130
for preliminary measures, as a member
of the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:32.140
So after class was over, as thanks
for letting me take a look at the textbook,

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:35.680
I thought about inviting him out to lunch.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:36.770
But...

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.650
I had second thoughts right before doing so.

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:44.690
I somehow...

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.900
...had a bad feeling about it.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:25.290
Well, Mayumi, I think you need to
take good heed of instincts like that.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:28.840
There were lots of times when I thought,
"Huh? Are these guys kidnappers?"

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.590
And they turned out to be kidnappers in the end.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:34.300
I think it's strange
if it happened multiple times.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:40.350
By the way, I wonder what the condition was
when Naganawa was run over.

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:43.310
I heard she didn't remember it clearly.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:45.690
Michiru looked into that already.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:50.070
When everything's said and done,
he's the one most fit to be a detective.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:57.740
Wana was talking to one of her
female friends on her cellphone

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:02.830
when she walked across the crosswalk
and a car that ran a red light ran her over.

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:12.550
The accident didn't have any eyewitnesses,
but how do you say it, there was an earwitness.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.380
But if it's through a cellphone,

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:19.010
there's no way to figure out things like
the car model, its license plates,

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:21.060
or the appearance of the driver.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:25.980
I'm also reluctant on leaving everything
about our sleuthing to Mr. Delinquent.

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:33.610
Hey, Mr. Bare-Legs, can we take a detour?

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:40.740
D Hill, the location of the problem,
is an uphill one-way street.

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:48.250
Come on now, why did you guys come here?

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.630
It's dangerous.
You should head straight home.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:56.800
Well, as you can see, D Hill is unpopular
so there should be no problems!

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:59.550
Unfortunately, it was a wasted effort.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:03.640
I looked around this entire area,
but I couldn't figure anything out.

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:11.770
So Wana was run over when she was walking
across this crosswalk while on the phone, right?

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:16.820
Then I'd imagine that she had fallen
somewhere around there?

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.660
Or around here, maybe.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:20.870
It's not like there's a line drawn in chalk,

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:24.950
or blood spatters anywhere,
so I can't say for certain.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:29.500
If she was run over by a car,
wouldn't she be sent flying, though?

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:32.630
If she was sent flying
and had slammed against the asphalt,

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:35.960
Wana wouldn't be safe and sound at all.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.380
Maybe the accident was something

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:40.840
where the foot was on the brakes,
and the impact was just a tap?

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:45.390
Then, at the least, there was no intent to kill?

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.810
So in reality it was just to scare her off,

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:51.730
and there was no intention of running her over,
but they screwed up and ended up hitting her?

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.490
Hey, Leader?

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.250
President?

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:12.330
BICYCLES 
REDUCE 
YOUR
 SPEED!!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:19.880
There you are, Leader.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.640
Oh, Mayumi!

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:26.270
If you've come here too, then that means
you were thinking the same thing I was!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:33.230
I was thinking I should verify which way
the car went after running over her.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.480
Which way it went...

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:38.740
In other words, where did it run off to.

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:41.360
Since this is a one-way street,

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:45.870
let's say it went straight and climbed all
the way up to the junction with this boulevard.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:50.120
Then, did it turn left or right?

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.880
No, those aren't the only options.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:55.340
It's the culprit of a hit-and-run,

00:21:55.340 --> 00:22:00.720
so they might commit a traffic violation along
the lines of running the wrong way on a one-way.

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:02.430
Yes, that's right.

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:06.140
I didn't even think about going
the wrong way on a one-way.

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:07.640
My hat's off to you, Mayumi!

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:12.940
Well, um, this isn't
what you can call a deduction.

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:18.400
Unfortunately, I am not learned.
What I have is just aestheticism.

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:24.530
Our leader spouted off his usual pet phrase.

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:29.660
But in this case, perhaps what he lacked
wasn't learning, but malice.

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:32.120
He naturally thought that
even a hit-and-run driver

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:36.880
who ran a red light would follow traffic signs.

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:40.300
For this case,
I can't expect a beautiful mystery

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:44.550
nor a beautiful answer
that would strike a chord with our leader.

00:22:48.930 --> 00:22:51.890
And that was when I suddenly realized it.

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:55.310
The reason why Mr. Senpai

00:22:55.310 --> 00:22:59.230
was trying to keep the school style
at status quo even after his graduation.

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:04.200
Even if it meant, of all things,
appointing my scummy self as his successor.

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:07.280
The reason why he is patiently and tenaciously

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:10.910
continuing to negotiate with
the efficiency-seeking academy.

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:19.000
It's probably for when this leader
of ours, currently a 5th grader,

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:23.590
can have even the smallest bit
of freedom and individuality...

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:30.640
...when he enters middle school.

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:36.010
EPISODE 10

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:36.010
